<code>assert (0 <= index && index <= size()) => (obj == null ? this.get(index) == null : this.get(index).equals(obj));</code>
--------------------
<code>assert 0 <= index && index <= size() => (obj == null ? this.get(index) == null : this.get(index).equals(obj));</code>
--------------------
<code>assert 0 <= index && index <= size() => (obj == null) == (this.get(index) == null) || this.get(index).equals(obj);</code>

However, the provided specification seems a bit off because the `add` method inserts the element at the specified index, shifting the element currently at that position (if any) and any subsequent elements to the right. Therefore, the correct specification should reflect that the element at the specified index after the addition should be equal to the object being added.

Here's the corrected version:

<code>assert 0 <= index && index <= size() => this.get(index).equals(obj);</code>
